            "props": {
              "body": "Topology of moonlighting proteins across interactomes"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "caption",
            "props": {
              "body": "Moonlighting protein set: **Curated**."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "caption",
            "props": {
              "body": "Each analysis defines its comparison background or random-set null model in its explanation. Unlabelled network proteins are not validated non-moonlighting controls. Results are cached in `data/cache/` and `data/analysis_runs/`."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "expander",
            "props": {
              "label": "How to read effects, significance and missing results",
              "expanded": false,
              "type": "default"
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "info",
                "props": {
                  "body": "Read effect direction and magnitude together with sample size and adjusted significance. Topology describes network associations; it does not validate moonlighting."
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "markdown",
                "props": {
                  "body": "Stars use BH-adjusted q-values: `*` q < 0.05; `**` q < 0.01; `***` q < 0.001; `****` q < 0.0001. `ns` means a valid test did not pass q < 0.05; `n/a` or an empty cell means the test or value is unavailable. Neither establishes equality. Captions and test tables identify comparisons and correction families. Descriptive curves, PCA coordinates and confidence scores receive no invented significance stars."
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "markdown",
                "props": {
                  "body": "Background proteins are unlabelled, not validated negatives. Source comparisons exclude the union from their shared background; hub tests use the full finite-valued network. Differences between interactomes can reflect assay design, coverage and filtering. Check finite sample counts and full test tables when values are sparse or unavailable."
                }
              }
            ]
          },
