          {
            "type": "expander",
            "props": {
              "label": "Analysis scope and reproducibility",
              "expanded": false,
              "type": "default"
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "markdown",
                "props": {
                  "body": "Every analysis runs separately on each selected network, with that network’s proteins as population. Where several networks are shown together, Benjamini–Hochberg is recomputed across all networks in the view (GO enrichment keeps one family per network because each network is its own universe). Each run saves CSV tables, parameters, network fingerprints, protein set accessions and the random seed in `data/analysis_runs/`. Advanced analyses are limited to networks with at most 500,000 edges. Degree bins are a practical adjustment, not exact degree matching."
                }
              },
